  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "xq+L0YCDu5ZUQsw5ydWiNCOjFhQ=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:38:11.636Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Authentication runs at the HTTP edge but resolvers need its result, and `reactor-api` threads it with a `WeakMap` keyed on the Fetch API `Request` object:\n\n```ts\ninterface AuthContext { user?: User; admins: string[]; auth_enabled: boolean; }\ntype AuthFetchMiddleware = (handler: FetchHandler) => FetchHandler;\n```\n\nThe flow: the HTTP adapter bridges the framework request into a Fetch `Request`; `authFetchMiddleware` calls `AuthService.authenticateRequest(request)` \u2014 an **invalid token returns a 401 immediately**, while a valid token or no token yields an `AuthContext`; the middleware does `authContextMap.set(request, authCtx)` and calls the wrapped handler; the gateway's `contextFactory(request)` does `getAuthContext(request)` and builds the GraphQL `Context { user, isAdmin, headers, db, \u2026 }`.\n\nTwo properties make this better than the alternatives. Because **the same `Request` instance** travels from `mount()` through to `createHandler()`, the lookup is guaranteed to find the context \u2014 without mutating shared state or threading an extra argument through every signature. And `WeakMap` entries are **garbage-collected with the `Request`**, so there is no manual cleanup and no leak on a long-lived server.\n\nTwo API notes: `getAuthContext` is deliberately **not exported** from the package index \u2014 it is an internal coupling point between `auth-middleware.ts` and `graphql-manager.ts`; and `AuthService.authenticate()`, the old Express middleware signature, is kept for backwards compatibility but is `@deprecated` in favour of `authenticateRequest()`.\n\nThe middleware's own branch table is the authoritative answer to \"when is there no user\": auth disabled, an `OPTIONS`/`GET` request, or no token \u2014 all produce a context without a user; only a **bad** token short-circuits with a 401.\n\n## Provenance\n- `packages/reactor-api/ARCHITECTURE.md` \u2014 Auth threading (types, how it works, WeakMap lifecycle); Request lifecycle\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:38:11.636Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:38:11.636Z"
    }
  },
